From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:49:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6351-fuel-gauge: announce the first headroom
 value

The headroom reads -ENODATA until the first counter window closes, and
then raised an event only when it moved a band from the first value. A
CPU limit that reads current_max on battery events therefore saw no
headroom at boot and capped nothing until an unrelated event: on one
boot the first cap came 155 s after start.

Raise an event when the headroom first becomes valid. The band and
30-second rules apply from there.
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
index e3ecf8f..f8dce52 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
@@ -467,8 +467,10 @@ static void mt6351_fg_headroom(struct mt6351_fg *fg)
 	 * every crossing of a band edge, and no more than one per interval.
 	 */
 	if (!fg->headroom_valid) {
+		/* The first value is news too: a limit may be waiting for it. */
 		fg->headroom_notified_ua = fg->headroom_ua;
 		fg->headroom_notified = now;
+		fg->headroom_changed = true;
 	} else if (abs(fg->headroom_ua - fg->headroom_notified_ua) >= MT6351_FG_HEADROOM_BAND_UA &&
 		   ktime_ms_delta(now, fg->headroom_notified) >= MT6351_FG_HEADROOM_EVENT_MS) {
 		fg->headroom_notified_ua = fg->headroom_ua;
